  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1145 AM CST Sun Nov 1 2026\n\nWith the full exit of the low pressure system late Monday into\nearly Tuesday, most models do expected a very brief break in the\nform of a passing ridge for Tuesday. This ridge should allow for a\nbit of drier conditions for the day as chance of precipitation\ndrop below 10 percent by sunrise that morning. However,\ntemperatures will stay cool with afternoon highs in the upper 50s\nto 60s for the day. Moving into Wednesday and rest of the work\nweek does look see the Panhandles return to our active pattern as\nmodels try to force a series of troughs and associated upper-level\nlows across the Panhandles. As of this morning, present long-term\nmodels have settled into better agreement on the first of these\ntroughs with present agreement looking to push in it across late\nWednesday. From here models have seen another ridge build behind\nthis trough giving us another break to close out the work week.\nBeyond this break, models have hinted at another trough following\nthis weekend. However, there is still a lot of disagreement on the\nactual strength of the trough by the time it arrives in the\nPanhandles. For now, present ensembles have chances of\nprecipitation across the Northern Panhandles at around 10 to 30\npercent for Wednesday. Meanwhile, the secondary system is only\nsitting at around a 10 to 15 percent chances given the still\npresent uncertainty. Otherwise, look for temperatures to stay on\nthe cooler side, with afternoon highs in the 60s to low 70s.",
